message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Clarvia Graph: Open Consequence Graph and Global Guidance Corpus for Terminal Illness and Bereavement Administration"
type: software
version: "0.1.0-alpha.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20572455"
date-released: "2026-06-06"
license: EUPL-1.2
url: "https://clarvia.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/clarvia-org/clarvia-graph"
abstract: >-
  An open, source-backed consequence graph and global multilingual guidance
  corpus (1,000 localized pages across 196 countries, 200 cross-border
  corridors, and 14 languages) modelling administrative workflows triggered by
  terminal illness and bereavement. Maps official government sources to
  structured tasks, deadlines, conditions, and evidence requirements. Aligned
  with CPSV-AP, CCCEV, ELI, and PROV-O.
authors:
